From abc1412103bcf632b9aa402cc2d665d0246b3895 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:49:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sx8-int8 attempt D: two-digit activations only for outlier
 blocks, skip kernel for the second pass

GGML_ARIFI_SX8_CM1_2D_GATE=<T>: for the two-digit S-X8 roles, the residual quantizer (quantize_q8_1 GATE spec
constant) writes the second digit only for q8_1 blocks with amax > T * mean|x|; all other blocks get q2 = 0, d2 = 0
(they stay one-digit). Pass 2 runs matmul_sx8skip_q8_1 (SX8_SKIP): each workgroup scans the residual block scales
of its column tile into a shared k-step bitmask and runs only the k-steps with a non-zero residual block. Pipelines
under key {SX8, Q8_0}. Default unchanged (gate 0 = fix B). Exactness controls: T=1 must equal fix B, a huge T must
equal one-digit. Offline (25 captured inputs): ffn_up at T=20 flags 0-0.42% of blocks, 0-4.4% of tile-chunks.

Lane: sx8-int8-stage10-2026-10-02

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
